I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services such as VirusTotal from this environment.  
If you run the following request yourself (using your API key `my_api`), you’ll get the related object IDs for the subdomains of `example.org`:

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/relationships/subdomains?limit=10&continuation_cursor=abc
Authorization: Bearer my_api
```

The response will look something like this (only the IDs and any context attributes are shown):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "subdomain1.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000000,
        "last_analysis_results": { ... }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "subdomain2.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000001,
        "last_analysis_results": { ... }
      }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "meta": {
    "continuation_cursor": "def"
  }
}
```

Replace the ellipses (`...`) with the actual data returned by the API. If you need help parsing the response or handling pagination, let me know!
